# Implementation Plan: Fix Photo Upload & Live Satellite Fetching

## Problem Statement

1. **Photo Upload Issue**: When a user uploads a satellite image, Streamlit re-executes `if uploaded_file is not None:` on every rerun. Because the file stream pointer wasn't reset to `0` and session state didn't track processed upload IDs, subsequent passes read 0 bytes (`b""`), causing inference errors or infinite rerun loops.
2. **Live Data Fetch Issue**: Live satellite imagery fetched via Esri/Yandex returns raw PNG/JPG byte arrays without spatial metadata. As a result, `run_scene_inference` generated lake coordinates in pixel space `(0-1024)` instead of real WGS84 coordinates `(36.58°N, 74.65°E)`. Folium map ignored these out-of-bounds pixel coordinates, causing the live map to display zero markers.

---

## Proposed Technical Changes

### 1. Robust File Upload Handler

#### [MODIFY] [load_upload.py](file:///d:/MUJ/Glacier%20lake/Glacier%20lake/src/inference/load_upload.py)
- Ensure `file_source.seek(0)` is invoked before reading file buffers (`BytesIO` / UploadedFile) so image data is always read completely.

#### [MODIFY] [app.py](file:///d:/MUJ/Glacier%20lake/Glacier%20lake/dashboard/app.py)
- Add upload state tracking `st.session_state["active_upload_id"]`. When a user picks a file, compute `upload_id = f"{uploaded_file.name}_{uploaded_file.size}"`.
- Only trigger U-Net segmentation when `active_upload_id` changes, avoiding endless reruns and repeated file reading.

---

### 2. Geographic Affine Transform for Live Satellite Imagery

#### [MODIFY] [satellite.py](file:///d:/MUJ/Glacier%20lake/Glacier%20lake/src/inference/satellite.py)
- Compute exact WGS84 geographic bounding box and `rasterio.Affine` transform for fetched satellite scenes using center `(lat, lon)`, `zoom`, and `size`:
  $$\text{DEG\_PER\_PIXEL\_LAT} = \frac{360.0}{256.0 \cdot 2^{\text{zoom}}}$$
  $$\text{DEG\_PER\_PIXEL\_LON} = \frac{\text{DEG\_PER\_PIXEL\_LAT}}{\max(\cos(\text{lat}_{\text{rad}}), 10^{-6})}$$
  $$\text{min\_lon} = \text{lon} - \frac{W \cdot \text{DEG\_PER\_PIXEL\_LON}}{2}, \quad \text{max\_lat} = \text{lat} + \frac{H \cdot \text{DEG\_PER\_PIXEL\_LAT}}{2}$$
  $$\text{Affine}( \text{DEG\_PER\_PIXEL\_LON}, 0, \text{min\_lon}, 0, -\text{DEG\_PER\_PIXEL\_LAT}, \text{max\_lat} )$$
- Return `(rgb_array, source_name, transform)` from `fetch_satellite_scene`.

#### [MODIFY] [run_inference.py](file:///d:/MUJ/Glacier%20lake/Glacier%20lake/src/inference/run_inference.py)
- Accept optional `override_transform` and `override_crs` parameters so fetched RGB images produce real geographic coordinates in `mask_to_geodataframe`.

#### [MODIFY] [app.py](file:///d:/MUJ/Glacier%20lake/Glacier%20lake/dashboard/app.py)
- Pass `transform` and `crs="EPSG:4326"` during live satellite scene inference.
- Use user settings (`threshold`, `min_area`, `enable_cloud_filter`) instead of hardcoded defaults.

